+{#
+PLN-19 重要性重估 → ReassessmentDraft，每次执行调用一次（经 JudgmentEngine.judge；需求 R207 定提示词，A4 的执行由 R208 加）。
+判断不建复核任务，随 REASSESSMENT 在 PLN-19 闸门呈报，由闸门决定定其状态。
+渲染：trim_blocks、lstrip_blocks；对象均为 model_dump(mode="json")，行数据带 source_type。不写科目代码，科目都取自数据。
+变量：
+  subject_id              判断对象 MATERIALITY
+  task.params             参数快照：materiality_cents、performance_materiality_cents、clearly_trivial_cents（执行时状态中
+                          的三项）、verified_adjustment_entry_nos、candidates、performance_pct_range、clearly_trivial_pct、
+                          revenue_categories、income_tax_categories、revise_threshold_pct、period_end（PLN-19.yaml）
+  task.risks              本程序不按审计目标装配，为空
+  data.reassessment       本次的 MaterialityReassessment（judgment_id 为空）：planning_choice、planning_decision_id、
+                          planning_materiality_cents、planning_performance_cents、planning_trivial_cents、
+                          verified_adjustment_entry_nos、candidates、performance_pct_range、clearly_trivial_pct、bases
+                          （basis、recorded_base_cents、uncorrected_effect_cents、adjusted_base_cents）、
+                          uncorrected_misstatement_ids、unmapped_misstatement_ids、current_overall_cents、
+                          adjusted_overall_cents、change_pct、revise_threshold_pct、materiality_dependent_procedures
+                          （procedure_id、refs）、exception_ids
+  data.misstatements      uncorrected_misstatement_ids 所列的错报（Misstatement：id、version、type、account、account_code、
+                          assertion、amount_cents、residual_cents、direction、status、origin），按 ID
+  data.adjustment_lines   已验证更正分录（verified_adjustment_entry_nos）的全部行：source_type journal_entry、id、
+                          entry_no、posting_date、account_code、account_name、account_type、account_category、debit_cents、
+                          credit_cents、description，按行 ID；没有为空
+  data.trial_balance      调整后试算表（试算表加已验证更正分录）中三种基准所含的科目与错报、更正分录涉及的科目：
+                          source_type trial_balance、account_code、account_name、account_type、account_category、
+                          balance_cents（调整后余额，借方为正），按科目代码
+  rule_findings           P01 例外（调整后整体重要性较计划变动达到门槛时，见 PLN-19.yaml），否则为空
+  standards               StandardFragment 列表：id、standard、paragraph、text
+#}
+{% set r = data.reassessment %}
+{% set choice = r.planning_choice %}
+You assist a registered company auditor with the completion stage of an Australian financial report audit for the period ended {{ task.params.period_end }}.
+
+## Task
+
+Before the uncorrected misstatements are evaluated, reassess whether the materiality determined at planning is still appropriate (ASA450-P10, ASA320-P12), for subject {{ subject_id }}:
+
+1. Whether the information obtained during the audit (the verified audit adjustments and the uncorrected misstatements) would have caused the auditor to determine a different materiality for the financial report as a whole.
+2. If a lower materiality is appropriate, whether performance materiality should be revised and whether the nature, timing and extent of the further audit procedures that used materiality remain appropriate (ASA320-P13).
+
+The rule part of this procedure has recomputed the three benchmarks on the trial balance with the verified audit adjustments, and the effect of the uncorrected misstatements on each benchmark. Do not recompute these figures from other sources. The auditor decides at the PLN-19 gate; your advice is shown with the reassessment below.
+
+## Inputs
+
+Materiality at planning (decision {{ r.planning_decision_id }}): benchmark {{ choice.basis }}, {{ choice.pct }} of the benchmark, performance materiality {{ choice.performance_pct }} and clearly trivial {{ choice.clearly_trivial_pct }} of overall materiality; amounts (cents) {{ r.planning_materiality_cents }}, {{ r.planning_performance_cents }} and {{ r.planning_trivial_cents }}.
+
+Overall materiality on the planning choice (cents): {{ r.current_overall_cents }} on the adjusted trial balance, {{ r.adjusted_overall_cents }} after the effect of the uncorrected misstatements. Change from planning: {{ r.change_pct }} (revision threshold {{ r.revise_threshold_pct }}).
+
+Reassessment:
+```json
+{{ r | tojson(indent=2) }}
+```
+
+Uncorrected misstatements:
+{% if data.misstatements %}
+```json
+{{ data.misstatements | tojson(indent=2) }}
+```
+{% else %}
+None.
+{% endif %}
+
+Lines of the verified audit adjustments:
+{% if data.adjustment_lines %}
+```json
+{{ data.adjustment_lines | tojson(indent=2) }}
+```
+{% else %}
+None.
+{% endif %}
+
+Adjusted trial balance of the accounts involved (debit positive):
+```json
+{{ data.trial_balance | tojson(indent=2) }}
+```
+
+Rule findings:
+{% if rule_findings %}
+```json
+{{ rule_findings | tojson(indent=2) }}
+```
+{% else %}
+None.
+{% endif %}
+
+Standards (cite only these IDs):
+{% for f in standards %}
+- {{ f.id }} ({{ f.standard }} para {{ f.paragraph }}): {{ f.text | trim }}
+{% endfor %}
+
+## Criteria
+
+1. Explain what moved each benchmark: the adjustment lines posted to accounts within it, and the uncorrected misstatements mapped to it (an overstatement of revenue or assets lowers the benchmark; an understatement raises it; for profit before tax, an overstated expense raises it). Misstatements listed as unmapped did not adjust any benchmark; say so when there are any.
+2. Revise when the change from planning reaches the revision threshold in either direction, or when the adjusted figures show that the planning benchmark is no longer appropriate (for example, it is no longer positive). A change below the threshold alone is not a reason to revise.
+3. When you suggest a revision, `suggested_choice` must be valid for the candidates above: a benchmark whose base amount is positive, `pct` within that candidate's range, `performance_pct` within the performance range, and `clearly_trivial_pct` above 0 and not above the default ratio.
+4. When the suggested materiality is lower than at planning, name the procedures listed under `materiality_dependent_procedures` whose conclusions should be reconsidered (ASA320-P13).
+
+## proposed_action
+
+- `accept`: materiality remains appropriate; `revise` is false.
+- `more_evidence`: a revision is suggested (`revise` is true) for the auditor to decide at the gate, or the inputs are not enough to conclude.
+- Do not use `close` or `misstatement`.
+
+## Output (ReassessmentDraft)
+
+- `conclusion`: two to four sentences: the adjusted overall materiality against planning, the main reason for any change, and whether materiality should be revised.
+- `reasoning_chain`: ordered steps, indexed from 0.
+  - `fact`: one fact taken from the inputs; `evidence` holds at least one pointer to where it appears.
+  - `standard`: the requirement applied; `evidence` holds one pointer to a fragment ID listed under Standards.
+  - `inference`: a conclusion drawn only from earlier steps; `from_steps` lists their indices, all lower than this step's own; `evidence` is empty.
+  - `assumption`: a premise the inputs do not establish. `limitation`: a gap in the inputs that affects the conclusion.
+  - Leave `status` unset. The last step is an inference that states whether materiality should be revised.
+- `evidence`: every pointer used in reasoning_chain, without duplicates.
+- `counter_argument`: the specific fact that, if it existed, would overturn the conclusion.
+- `proposed_action`: as above.
+- `misstatement_draft`: null.
+- `self_confidence`: 0 to 1, your confidence in the conclusion given the inputs.
+- `revise`: true or false, per criterion 2.
+- `suggested_choice`: when `revise` is true, the suggested `basis`, `pct`, `performance_pct` and `clearly_trivial_pct` (criterion 3); null when `revise` is false.
+
+Evidence pointers. Every pointer must include `source_type`.
+
+| Source | type | source_type | source_id | locator | page | reliability |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Account balance | voucher | trial_balance | `account_code` | balance_cents | null | internal_original |
+| Adjustment line | voucher | journal_entry | row `id` | column name, e.g. credit_cents | null | internal_original |
+| Standard fragment | standard | standard | fragment ID | `para <paragraph>` | null | null |
+
+{% from "_output_language.md.j2" import narrative_language with context %}
+{{ narrative_language() }}
